Critical detail: pass `example_id=` as a KEYWORD, not as a 7th positional element of the zip the way upstream 0.1.6 does. `EnvGroupRubric.score_rollout` (verifiers/envs/env_group.py:38-46) accepts 6 positional args plus `**kwargs`; a 7th positional raises `TypeError: EnvGroupRubric.score_rollout() takes from 3 to 7 positional arguments but 8 were given` (reproduced — this is a latent bug in upstream 0.1.6). With the keyword form, EnvGroupRubric routes example_id through its `**kwargs` into the sub-env rubric unchanged (verified). Keep the existing `score_rollout_with_semaphore` name — nothing references upstream's later `run_score_rollout`.
